Chapter: DeskWelcomeScaleTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 WORKS-53. Is the welcome frame's scale REDUCTION reachable at a supported
 geometry. It gates WORKS-52: `dk-win-y` reserves chrome at the frame's own
 `dk-win-s` scale and `dk-cbox-y` reserves it at `ui-scale w`, and those two
 differ only when `dk-win-s` has reduced, so the repair is inert if the
 reduction is unreachable and a second live defect if it is not.

 THE HOSTILE ROW IS THE POINT, NOT THE SUPPORTED ONES. Every supported
 geometry answering "no reduction" is indistinguishable from an instrument
 that cannot say yes (L-FALSIF). The last row is a synthetic 1024x480 --
 expressible as `-gop-width 1024 -gop-height 480`, not a mode anything ships
 at -- chosen as the cheapest geometry where `ui-scale` still answers 2 and
 the frame cannot fit at 2. Its answer must differ from the rows above it.

 THE FACE HALF NEEDS A VOLUME AND THE BATTERY ATTACHES NONE. `dk-line-step`
 reads `gf-gh` when the face loaded and falls back to `dk-line-h * s` when it
 did not, so the two paths compute a different `dk-win-h` and the question has
 to be asked of both. The gated run records the no-volume line and proves
 nothing about the face (L-NAMED); run it against an image built by
 `build-boot-img.ps1` for those rows, the way `desk-leading-metrics` is run.

Section: Body

  dws-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dws-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

 `dws-expect` IS THE THREE-ARM VERSION `dk-win-s` USED TO BE, kept here on
 purpose. The `s - 1` arm was deleted with WORKS-52 because `ui-scale` answers
 1 or 2 and nothing else, so the arm is reachable only at `s = 2` where `s - 1`
 is 1 and the final `else 1` answers 1 as well. `agrees` is that claim being
 checked on every row rather than asserted once: it compares what the function
 does now against what the deleted arm would have made it do. Re-deriving the
 CURRENT two-arm shape here would be printing one road twice (L-BOTHARMS).

  dws-expect : Integer, Integer, GopFont, Integer -> Integer
  dws-expect (w) (h) (tf) (ds) =
    let s = ui-scale w
    in if dk-win-fits w h tf s ds then s
    else if s > 1 & dk-win-fits w h tf (s - 1) ds then s - 1
    else 1

  dws-row : Integer, Integer, GopFont, Integer -> Text
  dws-row (w) (h) (tf) (ds) =
    let s = ui-scale w
    in let got = dk-win-s w h tf ds
    in "  " & integer-to-text w & "x" & integer-to-text h
       & "  ui-scale " & integer-to-text s
       & "  win-h " & integer-to-text (dk-win-h tf s)
       & "  needs " & integer-to-text (dk-win-h tf s * s)
       & "  box-h " & integer-to-text (dk-cbox-h w h ds)
       & "  fits " & dws-yn (dk-win-fits w h tf s ds)
       & "  dk-win-s " & integer-to-text got
       & "  reduced " & dws-yn (got < s)
       & "  agrees " & dws-yn (got == dws-expect w h tf ds)

 Whether the `s - 1` arm can ever produce a value the final `else 1` would not
 is decidable without a screen, since `ui-scale` answers 1 or 2 and nothing
 else. The two candidate answers are printed side by side rather than the
 conclusion being asserted.

  dws-arm : Integer -> Text
  dws-arm (w) =
    let s = ui-scale w
    in "  w " & integer-to-text w
       & "  ui-scale " & integer-to-text s
       & "  s - 1 " & integer-to-text (s - 1)
       & "  else-arm 1"
       & "  distinguishable " & dws-yn (s - 1 /= 1)

 THE FACE MUST BE LOADED AT THE PPEM THIS WIDTH ASKS FOR, NOT AT ONE PPEM FOR
 THE WHOLE SWEEP. `dk-ui-ppem` answers 16 at 1600 and above and 14 below, so a
 sweep holding one face measures a configuration the desk never builds at four
 of its six widths. **This chapter did exactly that when it landed and a
 finding was published off the 640x480 row** (val, 2026-08-27, corrected the
 same day). The row that is wrong is the one where the two ppems disagree,
 which is every row under 1600, and it is wrong in the direction that
 manufactures a defect: a 16 pixel face where the desk would use 14.

  dws-face : Fat16Volume, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console, Device.Port] Nothing
  dws-face (vol) (w) (h) (ds) = act
    f <- gfont-load vol "CMUNSS.TTF" (dk-ui-ppem w)
    if f.gf-ok == False then print-line-uni ("  " & integer-to-text w & "x" & integer-to-text h & "  CMUNSS.TTF not loaded")
    else print-line-uni ("  ppem " & integer-to-text (dk-ui-ppem w) & " cell " & integer-to-text (f.gf-gh) & dws-row w h f ds)
  end

  dws-sweep : GopFont, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  dws-sweep (tf) (ds) = act
    print-line-uni (dws-row 640 480 tf ds)
    print-line-uni (dws-row 800 600 tf ds)
    print-line-uni (dws-row 1024 768 tf ds)
    print-line-uni (dws-row 1280 800 tf ds)
    print-line-uni (dws-row 1600 900 tf ds)
    print-line-uni (dws-row 1024 480 tf ds)
  end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in act
    print-line-uni "the s - 1 arm against the else arm:"
    print-line-uni (dws-arm 640)
    print-line-uni (dws-arm 1024)
    print-line-uni (dws-arm 1600)
    print-line-uni "faceless (no TTF on the ESP), last row is the control:"
    dws-sweep gfont-none ds
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    if m.gm-ok == False then print-line-uni "CMUNSS face: no FAT volume on the boot medium"
    else act
      print-line-uni "CMUNSS, each row at the ppem the desk loads for ITS OWN width:"
      dws-face (m.gm-vol) 640 480 ds
      dws-face (m.gm-vol) 800 600 ds
      dws-face (m.gm-vol) 1024 768 ds
      dws-face (m.gm-vol) 1280 800 ds
      dws-face (m.gm-vol) 1600 900 ds
      dws-face (m.gm-vol) 1024 480 ds
      print-line-uni "end"
    end
    end
  end

